Hey!

This is regulated by the Public Transport Act (§ 65) and displaying the full name is a legal requirement:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
 (11) If the ordering of the taxi transport and the calculation of the price is carried out by means of an information society service, the carrier must, in a form which can be reproduced in writing:
(1) inform the passenger, before the start of the journey, *of the driver's name and surname, photograph, the number of the service card*, the maximum fare including taxes, or, if the destination of the journey is not predetermined, inform the passenger of the components of the fare, the tariff on the basis of which the fare is calculated or any other basis for calculating the fare, in such a way that the passenger is able to calculate the final fare with sufficient accuracy;
(2) provide the passenger with a summary of the journey, including the driver's name and surname, photograph, service card number, vehicle registration number, date of provision of the service, the start and end times, the origin and destination of the journey, the total duration and length of the journey, the price of the service and the amount paid.
{panel}

Essentially the requirements are the same for the taxi service and ride-hailing service

