[~accountid:63a2c00015d69a40aa170e8b], [~accountid:6052891960d39e006f72f0f0] sharing some additional legal considerations as previously agreed.

*The general recommendations applicable to all countries:*

* We believe that invoicing should follow the legal set-up. From reclassification and legal POV, we think that incentives for couriers are separate marketing service (and not us paying for delivery service), therefore, we consider that a separate invoice should be issued by the provider of the services. However, this is up to the tax team to make a final decision regarding the separate invoice.
* We recommend to approach fleets and not individual couriers in the markets where we have a mixed supply.
* Advertising must not be must not be misleading, not disturb public order and traffic on the roads and not contain reference to alcohol, tobacco and other products that may be harmful (there are some other restrictions in relation to advertisement of various goods).

*RO:*

* it is no longer considered to be a bribery to approach couriers without fleet's consent, but if Bolt will pay anything directly to couriers bypassing fleet it will raise unfair competition questions. Therefore, incentives agreement needs to be agreed with the fleet directly;
* we need to check market share in cities where incentives will be available. If market share is above 40% this may be considered as an abuse of dominant position if the incentives are likely to induce exclusivity;
* fleets as service providers will need to pay advertising tax which is provided by the Fiscal Code and is set by each municipality between 1-3% of the value of the service. The agreement with the fleet should provide clearly that any remuneration includes any such tax.

*CZ:*

* participation must be voluntary;
* there should be no unreasonable contractual penalty;
* need to inform fleets that they may need an appropriate trade license for this activity (and add in the contract that they acknowledge that they are aware);

*SK:*

* fleets/drivers need to be registered for subject of business “Advertising, marketing, photography and information services, market research and public opinion” if placing stickers on cars is not connected to any KPIs. We can draw their attention to this in the agreement/T&Cs;
* any text supplementing Bolt logo must be in Slovak language. If we want to add text in English in addition to Slovak, English wording should follow Slovak wording and content must be identical to Slovak wording. Also, font should be the same or smaller than text in Slovak language.

I hope this helps. I will be closing CEE sub ticket as agreed, but please feel free to reach out when help from legal will be required.

