{quote}{color:#bf2600}*Can you confirm that the following would NOT be possible and I understand it right:*{color}

# *Data Identification and Segmentation:*
1. AI model is trained on vast amounts of data and would be anonymized and aggregated to the extent possible. It means that no direct identifiers would be fed in the AI model of Bolt. There is, of course, a risk that some data provided in the chat, like special categories of data, can be processed by AI model.{quote}

It is correct that *from the final model there is no way to extract personal information*, also:

* (/) Anonymization of phone numbers and email addresses we are able to automatically detect has been done → PII is replaced with random numbers and text.
e.g. [johndoe@gmail.com|mailto:johndoe@gmail.com] → 123mkijqw@gmail.com
* Direct identifiers like order ID, user name, would *NOT* be used to train the model.



{quote}# *Model Training Complexity:*
## Training data is typically transformed into abstract representations and embedded within the model's parameters. The process involves the data being transformed and integrated in a way that does not retain original data formats or structures. Thus, providing a "copy" of the trained data, as required by GDPR, becomes impractical and impossible for Bolt.{quote}

Correct



{quote}# *Security and Proprietary Concerns:*
## Releasing the trained data or detailed internal structures of the model can pose significant security risks and expose proprietary information. It could also lead to the unintended disclosure of personal data of other users.{quote}

As you know we have *NO* plans of releasing the data or the model to public. They will be used privately in Bolt. To address the concern, it would *not* be possible to extract PII from the model itself. The model only predicts the intent type of a provided message. It is a classifier, meaning it is *NOT* a chat/AI model and it *cannot create text* so it is not possible to expose personal data from the model.



{quote}# {color:#bf2600}*Would we somehow label/mark in Admin which users chats were used for the training of the model?*{color}
