There are a few amendments and some issues regarding GDPR and tax. I will provide the summary below and ask relevant teams for help to double check everything.

*This will be the regular process flow for campaigns involving random selection of winners:*

* Prepare T&Cs that describe the campaign and the nature, number and commercial value of the prizes;
* Translate T&Cs to Romanian;
* Notarise T&Cs before the start of the campaign;
* Upload T&Cs to the website (standard version of T&Cs, no need to upload notarised version);
* Publish announcement regarding the campaign including link to the T&Cs;
* Publish names of the winners and allocate prizes;
* Pay taxes if required.

*Things to keep in mind:*

* T&Cs have to be available to participants on our website for the entire duration of the campaign;
* We need to publish names of the winners after the campaign is over;
* We need to specify whether the value of the Prize includes VAT;
* Bolt has to pay tax unless the value of the Prize is less than 600 RON;
* In case there are complaints from the participants Bolt has to review these and resolve by a committee of 3 members.

*Specific things brought out by the external counsel:*

* Participants need to be 18 years old and be residents of Romania. Do we check that?
* If a participant has multiple accounts is he/she allowed to have multiple entries?
* In case Bolt will need to pay taxes we will need a copy of winner's ID. We don't have copy of their ID and without it we cannot verify whether the payment of tax will be performed correctly. However, I assume this is not an issue since I doubt that the value of the prize will exceed 600 RON (this is when obligation to pay taxes arises).

