Hi Hendrik!

Yesterday I had a call with the local OPS and Public Policy teams, and this is the information that I got:

* After the form has been filled the driver will receive an automatic SMS and Email from NotLost three times over 5 days;
* If the driver still doesn’t reply, the case gets automatically escalated to the local OPS;
* Local OPS tries calling the driver two times, meanwhile leaves comments about the status of the case in NotLost;
* If the driver still doesn’t pick up, local OPS marks a case in NotLost and lets the rider know that we couldn’t reach the driver.

This seems like a process as of now, it could be subject to change as I will try to look at it in more detail. In case of any changes/additions in the process, it will be announced to CS via the updates Slack channel.

I was informed that CS agents were granted access to view cases in NotLost for London, and in the future access to all the areas will be given. I am not sure about the ETA, the Public Policy team will let me know about it. 

Please let me know if this information answers your questions, thank you! ❤️

