:google-meet: Had a meeting with Public Policy and OPS on August 14th:

* Reviewed the maps together, discussed unclear points.

❓ *Questions/actions discussed during the meeting:*

* *The regions table in the* [*🇬🇧 Passenger lost an item*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/78772] *article is outdated* - shared the Google doc of the table for Craig and Karolina to review and add comments where something needs to change;
** There was also an issue raised about drivers having a license of one city but living in another - it means that if CS fills out the form according to the driver’s license area, the driver might have to travel long distances to bring the item to the needed hub even though there could be another hub which is much closer to where the driver lives. It was highlighted that these cases are pretty rare, however they are the most common for the drivers in *Wolverhampton* area - there is a possibility that we might add some extra steps for CS for that region only (to check the driver’s address and fill out the needed form accordingly).
* *Polina’s question was also discussed* - Craig promised to provide some data on how responsive the drivers are to the automatic messages from NotLost and how often we have drivers who don’t respond to SMS and emails from the form for 5 days;
* *What happens after the driver doesn’t respond to NotLost for 5 days?* 
** The case gets automatically escalated to the local OPS;
** Local OPS tries calling the driver two times, meanwhile leaves comments about the status of the case in NotLost;
** If the driver still doesn’t pick up, local OPS marks a case in NotLost and lets the rider know that we couldn’t reach the driver.

I was informed that CS agents were granted access to view cases+comments in NotLost for London, and in the future access to all the areas will be given. Craig promised to investigate the ETA and let me know.

* *Driver: I found an item in the vehicle* - What should be the process for when the driver reports finding the item in the vehicle and they know during which ride it was lost? Should CS reach out to the rider to confirm that it was indeed their lost item and then proceed with filling out the lost property form? Should the lost property form be filled out at all? - Craig will take a look at the map again and decide.

